{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Your enemy's ox.</b> With a chirik under the yod, and it is a participle, for the word ואָיַבְתִי (Exodus 22) is among the verbs that are intransitive, and the meaning is even though you know that he is your enemy; and likewise שונאך. And your enemy is said because it is proper to speak thus; likewise שונאך. Perhaps this passage comes if the ox and the donkey belonged to a poor person — your reward would be very great, for you fulfilled the commandment of HaShem, and also kindness to a poor person."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:31.943898988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}